WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.167 --> 00:00:03.303
-Every day,
more evidence emerges

00:00:03.303 --> 00:00:05.505
in the impeachment inquiry
into President Trump,

00:00:05.505 --> 00:00:07.540
including damming
new text messages.

00:00:07.540 --> 00:00:09.675
For more on this, it's time
for "A Closer Look."

00:00:09.675 --> 00:00:14.380 line:0%
[ Suspenseful theme plays ]
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:00:14.380 --> 00:00:16.349
As you'll recall,
this all started

00:00:16.349 --> 00:00:19.051
when we found out that,
on an official phone call,

00:00:19.051 --> 00:00:20.987
the president dangled hundreds
of millions of dollars

00:00:20.987 --> 00:00:23.456
in military aid to Ukraine
and, in return,

00:00:23.456 --> 00:00:25.791
asked the president of Ukraine
to gin up

00:00:25.791 --> 00:00:27.961
politically motivated
investigations by telling him,

00:00:27.961 --> 00:00:29.762
"I would like you
to do us a favor."

00:00:29.762 --> 00:00:32.065
Now, we already have
the notes from the call

00:00:32.065 --> 00:00:33.366
on a whistleblower's account

00:00:33.366 --> 00:00:34.734
that was deemed credible
and urgent,

00:00:34.734 --> 00:00:36.736
but, over the weekend,
things got even worse for Trump

00:00:36.736 --> 00:00:39.071
when a second whistleblower
came forward.

00:00:39.071 --> 00:00:41.040
-This morning,
more breaking news.

00:00:41.040 --> 00:00:43.109
ABC News has learned
that the legal team

00:00:43.109 --> 00:00:44.810
representing the first
whistleblower

00:00:44.810 --> 00:00:47.279
is now representing
a second whistleblower.

00:00:47.279 --> 00:00:50.416
Attorney Mark Zaid told me
that the second whistleblower

00:00:50.416 --> 00:00:51.917
is a member of the
intelligence community

00:00:51.917 --> 00:00:53.419
with firsthand information

00:00:53.419 --> 00:00:55.621
on some of the allegations
at issue.

00:00:55.621 --> 00:00:58.758
-I gotta say, I'm shocked there
are only two whistleblowers.

00:00:58.758 --> 00:01:00.326
[ Laughter ]
I mean, you could blow
the whistle

00:01:00.326 --> 00:01:01.394
on this guy constantly.

00:01:01.394 --> 00:01:02.962
He's like a soccer player
who runs

00:01:02.962 --> 00:01:04.964
down length of the field
with the ball in his hands

00:01:04.964 --> 00:01:06.298
and then throws it
into the net.

00:01:06.298 --> 00:01:09.869
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:09.869 --> 00:01:10.936
[as Trump]
What do you mean, offsides?

00:01:10.936 --> 00:01:13.105
Was I offsides?

00:01:13.105 --> 00:01:14.607
Now, Trump and many Republicans

00:01:14.607 --> 00:01:17.043
have tried a few different
arguments to defend his behavior

00:01:17.043 --> 00:01:18.478
and none of them
have been convincing.

00:01:18.478 --> 00:01:21.781
First, they argued that there
was no illegal quid pro quo

00:01:21.781 --> 00:01:24.250
because Trump literally
did not stay words quid pro quo

00:01:24.250 --> 00:01:26.052
on the phone call.
-The president didn't do

00:01:26.052 --> 00:01:28.521
a darn thing wrong. When you
look at that conversation,

00:01:28.521 --> 00:01:29.522
there's no threat.

00:01:29.522 --> 00:01:30.890
There's no quid pro quo.

00:01:30.890 --> 00:01:33.259
-There's no quid pro quo,
no demand,

00:01:33.259 --> 00:01:34.861
no pressure, no threat.

00:01:34.861 --> 00:01:36.295
-His claims were bogus.

00:01:36.295 --> 00:01:37.963
There was no quid pro quo.

00:01:37.963 --> 00:01:40.700
-The transcript comes out
and there is no quid pro quo.

00:01:40.700 --> 00:01:42.534
-I have zero problems
with this phone call.

00:01:42.534 --> 00:01:44.303
There is no quid pro quo.

00:01:44.303 --> 00:01:47.673
[ Laughter ]
-There was no threat.

00:01:47.673 --> 00:01:49.842
There was no quid pro quo

00:01:49.842 --> 00:01:51.110
[ Laughter ]
in this call.

00:01:51.110 --> 00:01:53.379
-There was no quid pro quo.

00:01:53.379 --> 00:01:54.680
[ Laughter ]
There was nothing.

00:01:54.680 --> 00:01:58.184
There was no quid pro quo,
at all.

00:01:58.184 --> 00:01:59.685
If you remember,
at the beginning,

00:01:59.685 --> 00:02:02.221
it was [slowly] quid pro quo.

00:02:02.221 --> 00:02:04.090
[ Laughter ]
-Okay. First of all,

00:02:04.090 --> 00:02:05.725
just the way he says it,

00:02:05.725 --> 00:02:07.694
you know he has no idea
what it means.

00:02:07.694 --> 00:02:10.129
[ Laughter ]
He says the words

00:02:10.129 --> 00:02:13.198
[as Trump, slowly]
quid pro quo

00:02:13.198 --> 00:02:16.002
the way you read a subway map
in a foreign country.

00:02:16.002 --> 00:02:17.070
[ Laughter ]

00:02:17.070 --> 00:02:20.940
[as Trump]
El treno por la aeroporto.

00:02:20.940 --> 00:02:22.007
Honey!

00:02:22.007 --> 00:02:23.409
I think it's this one.

00:02:23.409 --> 00:02:24.710
This uno.

00:02:24.710 --> 00:02:27.213
[ Laughter ]
Second, you don't need

00:02:27.213 --> 00:02:28.915
to literally say
the words quid pro quo

00:02:28.915 --> 00:02:30.550
for it to be a quid pro quo.

00:02:30.550 --> 00:02:33.318
It can be a crime, even if you
don't stay name of the crime

00:02:33.318 --> 00:02:34.521
while you're doing it.

00:02:34.521 --> 00:02:35.921
[ Laughter ]
You can still be busted

00:02:35.921 --> 00:02:37.824
for buying weed,
even if you don't say,

00:02:37.824 --> 00:02:40.293
"Hello, I'm interested in the
possession of cannabis, please."

00:02:40.293 --> 00:02:41.828
[ Laughter ]
"How much do you want?"

00:02:41.828 --> 00:02:43.763
"Well, my intend is
to distribute."

00:02:43.763 --> 00:02:45.197
[ Laughter ]

00:02:45.197 --> 00:02:46.466
But don't take it from me.

00:02:46.466 --> 00:02:48.067
Take it from republican
Senator Lindsey Graham,

00:02:48.067 --> 00:02:51.537
who said this about Bill
Clinton's impeachment in 1999.

00:02:51.537 --> 00:02:54.274
-He doesn't to have say,
"Go lie for me" to be a crime.

00:02:54.274 --> 00:02:56.041
You don't have to say,
"Let's obstruct justice"

00:02:56.041 --> 00:02:57.910
for it to be a crime.

00:02:57.910 --> 00:03:01.747
You judge people on their
conduct, not magic phrases.

00:03:01.747 --> 00:03:04.951
-Of course, if we did judge
Trump on magic phrases,

00:03:04.951 --> 00:03:07.520
that'd work, too, because
he says quid pro quo

00:03:07.520 --> 00:03:09.655
like he's casting a spell
at Hogwarts.

00:03:09.655 --> 00:03:12.724
[ Laughter ]
[as trump] Quid...pro...quo!

00:03:12.724 --> 00:03:15.661
Look! Look, everyone!

00:03:15.661 --> 00:03:21.100
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:03:21.100 --> 00:03:23.636
I just turned my bat
into a lawyer.

00:03:23.636 --> 00:03:26.639
[ Laughter ]

00:03:26.639 --> 00:03:29.475
Not all the way, but close.

00:03:29.475 --> 00:03:31.410
Not only was this obviously
a quid pro quo,

00:03:31.410 --> 00:03:33.312
but it turns out Trump
was basically dragging

00:03:33.312 --> 00:03:35.848
as many as countries as he could
into his political crusade

00:03:35.848 --> 00:03:37.616
to investigate Joe Biden
and prove

00:03:37.616 --> 00:03:39.151
that the Russian
investigation was somehow

00:03:39.151 --> 00:03:41.754
a deep state witch hunt
orchestrated by the Democrats.

00:03:41.754 --> 00:03:45.091
As we found out last week,
he also involved Australia,

00:03:45.091 --> 00:03:47.660
Italy, and the UK in his
personal political crusade.

00:03:47.660 --> 00:03:49.428
In fact, he specifically
asked the UK for help

00:03:49.428 --> 00:03:52.431
after they got their new
prime minister, Boris Johnson,

00:03:52.431 --> 00:03:53.999
who has been very
friendly to Trump.

00:03:53.999 --> 00:03:55.435
I mean, look at these two.

00:03:55.435 --> 00:03:56.703
[ Laughter ]

00:03:56.703 --> 00:03:58.170
This looks like an audition room

00:03:58.170 --> 00:04:00.073
where two
less-good-lookin' actors are

00:04:00.073 --> 00:04:01.707
about to lose out on a role

00:04:01.707 --> 00:04:02.809
to Nick Nolte.

00:04:02.809 --> 00:04:04.510
[ Laughter ]

00:04:04.510 --> 00:04:06.612
[as Trump] You also here
for "Prince of Tides"?

00:04:06.612 --> 00:04:08.080
Yeah, me, too.
I didn't --

00:04:08.080 --> 00:04:09.448
I didn't learn any lines.

00:04:09.448 --> 00:04:10.683
I'm just gonna make stuff up.

00:04:10.683 --> 00:04:12.017
[ Laughter ]

00:04:12.017 --> 00:04:14.220
Whoa!
These tides today, huh?

00:04:14.220 --> 00:04:15.721
[ Laughter ]

00:04:15.721 --> 00:04:19.458
[ Fresh laughter ]

00:04:19.458 --> 00:04:22.561
Lotta tides, yeah.

00:04:22.561 --> 00:04:23.796
Who's the girl in this movie?

00:04:23.796 --> 00:04:24.797
Barbra Streisand?!

00:04:24.797 --> 00:04:26.098
Oh [bleep] me!

00:04:26.098 --> 00:04:28.334
[ Boisterous laughter ]

00:04:28.334 --> 00:04:30.502
I'm never gonna get it now!

00:04:30.502 --> 00:04:32.438
[ Laughter fading ]

00:04:32.438 --> 00:04:35.708
[ Fresh laughter ]

00:04:35.708 --> 00:04:38.177
Then, last week, of course,
after involving Russia, Ukraine,

00:04:38.177 --> 00:04:39.345
Italy, Australia, and the UK

00:04:39.345 --> 00:04:40.579
in his personal
political vendettas,

00:04:40.579 --> 00:04:42.948
Trump just confessed on TV
and, for the hell of it,

00:04:42.948 --> 00:04:44.450
threw China in there, too.

00:04:44.450 --> 00:04:47.353
-What, exactly, did you
hope Zelensky would do

00:04:47.353 --> 00:04:49.288
about the Bidens
after your phone call?

00:04:49.288 --> 00:04:51.357
-Exactly!
-Well, I would think that,

00:04:51.357 --> 00:04:53.859
if they were honest about it,
they'd start

00:04:53.859 --> 00:04:56.562
a major investigation
into the Bidens.

00:04:56.562 --> 00:04:59.198
It's a very simple answer.

00:04:59.198 --> 00:05:01.200
They should investigate
the Bidens.

00:05:01.200 --> 00:05:03.635
Likewise, China should start

00:05:03.635 --> 00:05:05.771
an investigation
into the Bidens.

00:05:05.771 --> 00:05:07.807
-So, now, he's asking
China, too.

00:05:07.807 --> 00:05:10.376
At this point, it would be
easier for cable news shows

00:05:10.376 --> 00:05:12.912
to tell us which countries
Trump hasn't tried to extort.

00:05:12.912 --> 00:05:15.514
[ Laughter ]

00:05:15.514 --> 00:05:18.351
Now, Republicans --

00:05:18.351 --> 00:05:19.918
Republicans
first tried to argue

00:05:19.918 --> 00:05:21.754
there was no illegal
quid pro quo,

00:05:21.754 --> 00:05:24.457
but, now that he's literally
said the crime out loud on TV,

00:05:24.457 --> 00:05:25.491
you might be asking yourself,

00:05:25.491 --> 00:05:26.792
"How can they possibly
defend him?"

00:05:26.792 --> 00:05:28.794
Well, Republicans have come up
with a new defense:

00:05:28.794 --> 00:05:30.229
He was just joking.

00:05:30.229 --> 00:05:33.198
-Are you comfortable with what
the president has said here

00:05:33.198 --> 00:05:36.369
in this call for foreign
governments, Ukraine and China,

00:05:36.369 --> 00:05:38.404
to investigate
his political opponent?

00:05:38.404 --> 00:05:41.206
-Well, I doubt if the
China comment

00:05:41.206 --> 00:05:42.642
was serious,
to tell you the truth.

00:05:42.642 --> 00:05:44.143
[chuckling]
The president loves to go out

00:05:44.143 --> 00:05:46.011
on the White House driveway.

00:05:46.011 --> 00:05:47.180
I haven't talked
to him about this.

00:05:47.180 --> 00:05:49.081
I don't know what
the president was thinking,

00:05:49.081 --> 00:05:51.450
but I knew he loves
to bait the press.

00:05:51.450 --> 00:05:53.319
-Do you think it's appropriate
for President Trump

00:05:53.319 --> 00:05:56.889
to ask China and Ukraine
to investigate Joe Biden?

00:05:56.889 --> 00:05:58.991
-George, you really
think he was serious

00:05:58.991 --> 00:06:02.528
about thinking that China's
gonna investigate, uh,

00:06:02.528 --> 00:06:03.896
the Biden family?

00:06:03.896 --> 00:06:05.030
-I don't know if that's
a real request

00:06:05.030 --> 00:06:06.899
or him just needling the press,

00:06:06.899 --> 00:06:08.968
knowing that you guys were
gonna get outraged by it.

00:06:08.968 --> 00:06:10.402
I think he did it
to provoke you

00:06:10.402 --> 00:06:12.971
to ask me and others
and get outraged by it.

00:06:12.971 --> 00:06:14.474
-Yeah, but, come on,
he's the president.

00:06:14.474 --> 00:06:16.341
We have to take
his word seriously.

00:06:16.341 --> 00:06:18.510
It's not his job
to outrage people.

00:06:18.510 --> 00:06:20.046
You're talkin' about him
like he's some

00:06:20.046 --> 00:06:22.047
shock jock
with a morning radio show.

00:06:22.047 --> 00:06:23.782
[ Laughter ]
[as Trump] If you ask me,

00:06:23.782 --> 00:06:25.450
China should investigate Biden

00:06:25.450 --> 00:06:26.785
[ Siren wailing ]
and -- Oh!

00:06:26.785 --> 00:06:28.854
[ Laughter ]
You know what that sound means.

00:06:28.854 --> 00:06:30.455
It's time for the Wolf Pack
to call in

00:06:30.455 --> 00:06:31.857
with your sex questions.
-[Howling]

00:06:31.857 --> 00:06:34.059
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah! And, remember,

00:06:34.059 --> 00:06:35.461
whoever has
the dirtiest question

00:06:35.461 --> 00:06:37.830
wins two free tickets
to tonight's monster truck show.

00:06:37.830 --> 00:06:40.332
[ Engine revving,
air horn blaring ]

00:06:40.332 --> 00:06:44.069
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:06:44.069 --> 00:06:46.972
Of course, everyone

00:06:46.972 --> 00:06:49.108
knew what Trump was doing
when he was doing it.

00:06:49.108 --> 00:06:51.544
The president mysteriously
suspended hundreds of millions

00:06:51.544 --> 00:06:54.580
of dollars in military aid
that Ukraine desperately needed

00:06:54.580 --> 00:06:57.182
and then, he asked the president
of Ukraine to do us a favor

00:06:57.182 --> 00:06:58.918
by investigating
a political rival.

00:06:58.918 --> 00:07:01.086
At the same time, his personal
lawyer was going around

00:07:01.086 --> 00:07:03.655
telling reporters, "We're
meddling in an investigation.

00:07:03.655 --> 00:07:05.424
There's nothing illegal
about it.

00:07:05.424 --> 00:07:07.593
Someone could say
it's improper."

00:07:07.593 --> 00:07:09.428
[ Laughter ]
Somebody? How about everybody?

00:07:09.428 --> 00:07:10.997
[ Fresh laughter ]
I mean, even

00:07:10.997 --> 00:07:13.232
the president of Finland, when
he met with Trump last week,

00:07:13.232 --> 00:07:15.568
was like, "Get your crime
hand away from me!"

00:07:15.568 --> 00:07:17.135
[ Boisterous laughter
and applause ]

00:07:17.135 --> 00:07:19.672
Then --
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:07:19.672 --> 00:07:22.508
Then, on top of the facts
we already had,

00:07:22.508 --> 00:07:24.944
last week, we got newly
unearthed text messages

00:07:24.944 --> 00:07:27.512
from State Department officials
in which they made it very clear

00:07:27.512 --> 00:07:29.682
that they also knew
exactly what was going on.

00:07:29.682 --> 00:07:31.484
Now, as we established,
Rudy Giuliani,

00:07:31.484 --> 00:07:32.751
the president's personal lawyer,

00:07:32.751 --> 00:07:33.786
who is in no way
a government official,

00:07:33.786 --> 00:07:35.854
was basically acting
as the middle man

00:07:35.854 --> 00:07:37.656
between Trump and Ukraine
on all this,

00:07:37.656 --> 00:07:39.492
which, right off the bat,
is a terrible choice.

00:07:39.492 --> 00:07:41.260
I mean, that's like
if you were putting together

00:07:41.260 --> 00:07:43.829
a Ocean's 11-style team
for your bank heist

00:07:43.829 --> 00:07:45.664
and you chose,
as your computer expert,

00:07:45.664 --> 00:07:48.167
Frank Costanza.
[ Laughter ]

00:07:48.167 --> 00:07:50.002
Although, he'd still probably
be better than Rudy

00:07:50.002 --> 00:07:51.771
at giving Trump legal advice.

00:07:51.771 --> 00:07:53.439
-There was no quid pro quo.

00:07:53.439 --> 00:07:55.040
-You don't know
what the hell you're doin'!

00:07:55.040 --> 00:07:57.176
[ Laughter ]
-Now,

00:07:57.176 --> 00:08:00.912
[ Cheering and applause ]
Rudy has repeatedly insisted

00:08:00.912 --> 00:08:03.249
he was acting on orders
from the State Department

00:08:03.249 --> 00:08:05.218
and even going so far
as to go on Fox News

00:08:05.218 --> 00:08:07.520
and show them phone calls
and text messages

00:08:07.520 --> 00:08:09.855
from one State Department
official, in particular,

00:08:09.855 --> 00:08:11.023
named Kurt Volker.

00:08:11.023 --> 00:08:13.392
-You didn't get involved
on this on your own.

00:08:13.392 --> 00:08:16.194
Did our State Department ask you
to go on a mission for them?

00:08:16.194 --> 00:08:17.462
-They did.

00:08:17.462 --> 00:08:20.099
You know who I did it
at the request of?

00:08:20.099 --> 00:08:22.501
The State Department.
It's all here.

00:08:22.501 --> 00:08:24.336
Right here.
[ Laughter ]

00:08:24.336 --> 00:08:26.038
The first call
from the State Department.

00:08:26.038 --> 00:08:29.908
I went to meet
Mr. Zelensky's aide

00:08:29.908 --> 00:08:31.710
at the request
of the State Department.

00:08:31.710 --> 00:08:33.812
Here's Kurt saying,
"Great. I will tell Yermak

00:08:33.812 --> 00:08:35.914
and he'll visit with you there.
Thanks.

00:08:35.914 --> 00:08:38.684
Mr. Mayor, how was
your meeting with Andriy?

00:08:38.684 --> 00:08:40.586
Do you have time for a call?

00:08:40.586 --> 00:08:42.188
Best, Kurt."

00:08:42.188 --> 00:08:43.722
-Man, you know
you're a bad criminal

00:08:43.722 --> 00:08:46.258
when you keep the evidence
against you on multiple devices.

00:08:46.258 --> 00:08:48.361
[ Laughter ]
He's got a phone, an iPad.

00:08:48.361 --> 00:08:50.096
What's next?
Alexa, what's it called

00:08:50.096 --> 00:08:51.830
when you ask someone
to do a favor for you

00:08:51.830 --> 00:08:52.898
in exchange for money?

00:08:52.898 --> 00:08:55.301
-It's called a quid pro quo.

00:08:55.301 --> 00:08:56.669
[ Cheering and applause ]
Damn it!

00:08:56.669 --> 00:08:59.304
Now, Rudy pointed the blame

00:08:59.304 --> 00:09:01.273
directly at the
State Department, so, naturally,

00:09:01.273 --> 00:09:02.341
Democrats called Volker,

00:09:02.341 --> 00:09:03.575
the former State Department
official,

00:09:03.575 --> 00:09:05.978
to testify last week
and he revealed to them

00:09:05.978 --> 00:09:08.147
some incredibly damning text
messages that made it cheer

00:09:08.147 --> 00:09:09.848
that people
at the State Department

00:09:09.848 --> 00:09:11.617
knew exactly what was
happening at the time.

00:09:11.617 --> 00:09:13.819
In one text, Volker told
a Ukrainian official

00:09:13.819 --> 00:09:16.154
that a meeting with Trump
was basically contingent

00:09:16.154 --> 00:09:17.489
on the Ukrainian president

00:09:17.489 --> 00:09:19.358
doing the investigation
Trump wanted.

00:09:19.358 --> 00:09:20.693
-From Kurt Volker to

00:09:20.693 --> 00:09:23.995
Ukrainian presidential
advisor Andriy Yermak,

00:09:23.995 --> 00:09:26.131
it says, "Good lunch.
Thanks.

00:09:26.131 --> 00:09:27.532
Heard from White House.

00:09:27.532 --> 00:09:31.437
Assuming President Z convinces
Trump he will investigate,

00:09:31.437 --> 00:09:34.740
get to the bottom
of what happened in 2016,

00:09:34.740 --> 00:09:37.409
we will nail down date
for visit to Washington.

00:09:37.409 --> 00:09:39.945
Good luck.
See you tomorrow. Kurt."

00:09:39.945 --> 00:09:42.014
-They wrote it all down.
It's all right there.

00:09:42.014 --> 00:09:44.916
He even signs his name and says
"See you tomorrow. Kurt."

00:09:44.916 --> 00:09:46.552
[ Laughter ]
So weird.

00:09:46.552 --> 00:09:48.454
It's like if you left
a ransom note

00:09:48.454 --> 00:09:51.090
cut out from magazine letters
that said, "Give us the money

00:09:51.090 --> 00:09:52.491
or you'll never see
your son again.

00:09:52.491 --> 00:09:53.725
[ Laughter ]
Have a great weekend.

00:09:53.725 --> 00:09:54.893
Kurt the Kidnapper."

00:09:54.893 --> 00:09:56.862
[ Applause ]
But the text messages

00:09:56.862 --> 00:09:58.030
get even more --

00:09:58.030 --> 00:09:59.998
[ Applause ]

00:09:59.998 --> 00:10:01.701
Text messages get
even more explosive.

00:10:01.701 --> 00:10:03.202
For example, there's an exchange

00:10:03.202 --> 00:10:04.736
between two
State Department officials

00:10:04.736 --> 00:10:06.705
where one of them
expresses concern

00:10:06.705 --> 00:10:08.841
about what's going on
and the other one realizes

00:10:08.841 --> 00:10:10.509
they should not be texting
about this at all.

00:10:10.509 --> 00:10:11.943
-On September 1st,

00:10:11.943 --> 00:10:14.713
the top US diplomat
in Ukraine, Bill Taylor,

00:10:14.713 --> 00:10:18.216
texts the U.S. ambassador
to EU, Gordon Sondland,

00:10:18.216 --> 00:10:21.019
and writes this:
"Are we now saying

00:10:21.019 --> 00:10:23.823
that security assistance
and White House meetings

00:10:23.823 --> 00:10:25.991
are conditioned
on investigations?"

00:10:25.991 --> 00:10:28.527
Sondland says, "Call me."

00:10:28.527 --> 00:10:29.895
[ Laughter ]
-Damn.

00:10:29.895 --> 00:10:32.297
Anytime you text someone
and they respond by saying,

00:10:32.297 --> 00:10:34.800
"Call me," it is not good.
[ Laughter ]

00:10:34.800 --> 00:10:36.969
If you text a date,
"Looking forward to tonight,"

00:10:36.969 --> 00:10:38.370
and they text back, "Call me"...

00:10:38.370 --> 00:10:39.638
[ Laughter ]

00:10:39.638 --> 00:10:41.107
...that date is not happening.

00:10:41.107 --> 00:10:43.008
[ Laughter ]
The only thing worse is seein'

00:10:43.008 --> 00:10:44.476
those three bubbles
come up for a while

00:10:44.476 --> 00:10:45.878
as you just wait
for your response.

00:10:45.878 --> 00:10:47.245
Like, "I can see you typing.

00:10:47.245 --> 00:10:48.714
Are you still typing?

00:10:48.714 --> 00:10:50.783
How long is this message?
Are we committing a crime?

00:10:50.783 --> 00:10:53.552
[ Laughter ]
Oh, no!

00:10:53.552 --> 00:10:57.289
[ Fresh laughter ]
Ohhh, no! It is a crime!"

00:10:57.289 --> 00:11:00.092
[ Applause ]

00:11:00.092 --> 00:11:02.361
So, now, the second
whistleblower coming forward

00:11:02.361 --> 00:11:03.862
and all this new evidence
coming out,

00:11:03.862 --> 00:11:05.164
Trump's looking for a fall guy

00:11:05.164 --> 00:11:06.832
and, since he's
a political mastermind

00:11:06.832 --> 00:11:09.968
who, apparently, is an expert
at manipulating the press,

00:11:09.968 --> 00:11:12.104
he looked around and he
found the perfect guy.

00:11:12.104 --> 00:11:14.407
the guy who everyone
would definitely believe

00:11:14.407 --> 00:11:16.175
was responsible for all of this:

00:11:16.175 --> 00:11:18.210
Energy Secretary Rick Perry.

00:11:18.210 --> 00:11:20.178
-President Trump
has a new defense

00:11:20.178 --> 00:11:23.315
for his July 25th phone call
to the president of Ukraine

00:11:23.315 --> 00:11:24.449
that is at the center

00:11:24.449 --> 00:11:26.485
of House Democrats's
impeachment inquiry.

00:11:26.485 --> 00:11:29.188
Trump told House Republicans
Friday that he was urged

00:11:29.188 --> 00:11:32.792
to make the call
by Energy Secretary Rick Perry.

00:11:32.792 --> 00:11:35.394
Sources say Trump suggested
it was a call

00:11:35.394 --> 00:11:36.929
he didn't even want to make.

00:11:36.929 --> 00:11:38.730
-That's right.
He wants to us believe

00:11:38.730 --> 00:11:40.966
the mastermind behind all this
was Rick Perry.

00:11:40.966 --> 00:11:42.835
[ Laughter ]
I'm sorry, but people are not

00:11:42.835 --> 00:11:45.571
gonna believe Rick Perry is
the brains behind all of this

00:11:45.571 --> 00:11:47.372
because, what,
because he wears glasses?

00:11:47.372 --> 00:11:49.474
[ Laughter ]
But don't take it from me.

00:11:49.474 --> 00:11:50.609
Take it from this guy.

00:11:50.609 --> 00:11:52.644
-I see Rick Perry the other day.

00:11:52.644 --> 00:11:55.581
He put glasses on so people
will think he's smart.

00:11:55.581 --> 00:11:56.848
[ Laughter ]

00:11:56.848 --> 00:11:58.083
And it just doesn't work!

00:11:58.083 --> 00:12:00.118
You know, people can see
through the glasses.

00:12:00.118 --> 00:12:02.054
[ Laughter ]
-Trump probably forgot

00:12:02.054 --> 00:12:03.989
he said that, then saw
Rick Perry one day and said,

00:12:03.989 --> 00:12:05.090
[as Trump]
"That guy must be smart.

00:12:05.090 --> 00:12:07.192
He wears glasses.
[ Laughter ]

00:12:07.192 --> 00:12:08.961
All the evidence is right
in front of us.

00:12:08.961 --> 00:12:10.796
The president used his office
and the entirety

00:12:10.796 --> 00:12:12.064
of American foreign policy

00:12:12.064 --> 00:12:13.732
to pursue his personal
political goals

00:12:13.732 --> 00:12:15.434
and people knew, at the time,

00:12:15.434 --> 00:12:17.403
that it was an obviously
corrupt abuse of power.

00:12:17.403 --> 00:12:19.304
So, Republicans, of you're
confused about any of this,

00:12:19.304 --> 00:12:20.939
I'll say it very slowly.

00:12:20.939 --> 00:12:23.442
[as Trump, slowly]
This was a...

00:12:23.442 --> 00:12:25.410
-[slowly] Quid pro quo.

00:12:25.410 --> 00:12:26.745
-This has been "A Closer Look."

00:12:26.745 --> 00:12:30.750
[ Cheering and applause ]
♪♪

